**Version Used**: Visual Studio 2026 18.12.0

**Steps to Reproduce**:

1. Create a source generator that emits a `file`-local type:
   ```csharp
   [Generator]
   public sealed class GreetingGenerator : IIncrementalGenerator
   {
       public void Initialize(IncrementalGeneratorInitializationContext context)
       {
           context.RegisterPostInitializationOutput(c => c.AddSource("GreetingAttribute.g.cs", """
               namespace Demo;
               [System.AttributeUsage(System.AttributeTargets.Class)]
               internal sealed class GreetingAttribute(string text) : System.Attribute;
               """));

           var texts = context.SyntaxProvider.ForAttributeWithMetadataName(
               "Demo.GreetingAttribute",
               static (_, _) => true,
               static (ctx, _) => (string)ctx.Attributes[0].ConstructorArguments[0].Value!);

           context.RegisterSourceOutput(texts, static (c, text) => c.AddSource("Greeting.g.cs", $$"""
               namespace Demo;
               internal static class Greeting { public static void Print() => GreetingWriter.Write(); }
               file static class GreetingWriter { public static void Write() => System.Console.WriteLine("{{text}}"); }
               """));
       }
   }
   ```
2. Create a console app that references the generator (`OutputItemType="Analyzer" ReferenceOutputAssembly="false"`). Do not set `EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles`:
   ```csharp
   [Greeting("Hello, world!")]
   internal static class Program
   {
       private static void Main()
       {
           while (true) { System.Console.ReadKey(); Greeting.Print(); }
       }
   }
   ```
3. Build the solution, start the app with Hot Reload. Change the attribute text. Hot Reload applies the change, this is correct.
4. Stop the app. Add `<EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>true</EmitCompilerGeneratedFiles>` to the app project, then rebuild.
5. Start the app again and change the attribute text.

**Expected Behavior**:
The change is applied.

**Actual Behavior**:
