**Version Used**: the C# language server 5.13 (`roslyn-language-server` 5.13.0-1.26514.10), a project targeting `net10.0`.

**Steps to Reproduce**:

```csharp
// Program.cs (System.Linq is an implicit using)
using System.Linq;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

class C
{
    Task<string?> M(IQueryable<string> q) => q.FirstOrDefaultAsync();
}
```

```csharp
// Queries.cs
using System.Linq;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

namespace Queries;

public static class QueryableExtensions
{
    public static Task<T?> FirstOrDefaultAsync<T>(this IQueryable<T> source) => Task.FromResult(default(T));
}
```

**Expected Behavior**: Add Import offers `using Queries;` on `FirstOrDefaultAsync`, as it does when no method of that name is in scope (CS1061).

**Actual Behavior**: since .NET 10, `System.Linq.AsyncEnumerable.FirstOrDefaultAsync` is in scope through `System.Linq`, so the call binds to it and fails with CS0411 (its type arguments cannot be inferred from an `IQueryable<string>`). CS0411 isn't among `AddImportDiagnosticIds.FixableDiagnosticIds` (`CSharpAddImportCodeFixProvider.cs`), so no import is offered at any position on the call.

The common case is EF Core: `FirstOrDefaultAsync`, `ToListAsync`, `CountAsync`, `AnyAsync`, `SingleAsync` and the rest of `EntityFrameworkQueryableExtensions` on an `IQueryable` in a file without `using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;`. Before .NET 10 these gave CS1061 and Add Import offered the using; now they give CS0411 and nothing is offered.

Asking `IAddImportFeatureService.GetFixesAsync` for CS0411 the same way the provider asks it for CS1061 offers the right namespace (and only where one of its extension methods takes the receiver) in our tests, so adding CS0411 to the fixable ids may be enough.

`AppHostsAreGeneratedPerHostAndTypeLibraryIsIndependent` could intermittently miss apphost regeneration when a rewritten input and existing output had indistinguishable timestamps on Windows.

### Changes

- Added a helper that advances rewritten input timestamps beyond all current apphost outputs.
- Applied it to template, compiler, MSBuild, task, and HostModel input mutations.
- Preserved the assertion that unrelated layout task changes do not regenerate apphosts.

```csharp
while (File.GetLastWriteTimeUtc(path) <= latestHostTimestamp)
{
    WaitForUtcNowToAdvance();
    File.SetLastWriteTimeUtc(path, DateTime.UtcNow);
}
```

